SaturnSwap V3 order datum fixtures
==================================

Real mainnet SwapDatum CBOR (inline / datum-hash-resolved) captured from the V3
order script address and from the filler-repo cited on-chain proof transactions.
Captured via the public Koios mainnet API (no key).

V3 order script address:
  addr1z9sz8avaecqxfuwk6f6efkl2yk7yxpdf76ss7wsxgqm42wh2l9cdyhc0eja9mxq0lgeer90edhlfymnxv2ym3szcetqsp0ume8
  script hash: 6023f59dce0064f1d6d27594dbea25bc4305a9f6a10f3a064037553a

Each *.hex file is the raw datum CBOR hex on a single line (no trailing newline),
suitable for `bytes.fromhex(open(f).read().strip())` -> cbor2.loads / PlutusData.from_cbor.

Fixtures
--------

order_ad182bcd.hex
  Source: LIVE UTxO ad182bcd7273ed7130ac22568ee9ddb0890f90db7040dd68e2bafa69342805b3#0
          (resting at the V3 address at capture time; also the filler repo's
          partial-fill proof tx). Datum was INLINE on the live UTxO.
  Sell side: 1500 FRENCHIE WIFF (policy 50cd0a2d...89f8e, name 4652454e43484945205749464620),
             held UTxO value 2.1 ADA + the 1500 tokens.
  coverage = None (Constr 1 / tag 122)
  min_partial_fill = 1000000
  Carries a non-null seed order-ref (Constr 0): b6bcae...754cc index 2.

order_18a01339.hex
  Source: LIVE UTxO 18a0133987f8f2f308b5f62fb319d64a5276896585d35beab7efd8ea1edfd14e#0
          (resting at the V3 address at capture time). Datum was INLINE.
  UTxO value 10 ADA. Owner uses a SCRIPT payment credential (Constr 1 / tag 122,
  hash 7b3130ac...818db) with no stake part (Constr 1 / tag 122).
  coverage = None
  min_partial_fill = 0
  seed order-ref = all-zero placeholder, index 0.

order_b6bcaeb6_out0_cov_none.hex
  Source: create proof tx b6bcaeb69401127ed650fea550c87464c7fed8aeef05f25950738db6ece754cc,
          output #0 (and identical datum on #3). Resolved via datum_info by hash
          630e472394b0ab3751ac8c39990507c1f3556c3827757c70e3065255695b0b43
          (the create-tx outputs carried datum-hash, not inline).
  Sell 4.0 ADA -> buy 1000 FRENCHIE WIFF. coverage = None. min_partial_fill = 0.

order_b6bcaeb6_out2_cov_none.hex
  Source: create proof tx b6bcae... output #2. Resolved via datum_info by hash
          7669735d2bb00ed29d1e664a3846a31e8747e1f9d9ee0d2cf0a77da3b5465e0c.
  Buy 3000 FRENCHIE WIFF for 6.0 ADA (sell side). coverage = None.
  min_partial_fill = 1000000. Same field ordering as order_ad182bcd.

order_b6bcaeb6_out1_cov_some.hex  <-- the coverage=Some fixture
  Source: create proof tx b6bcae... output #1. Resolved via datum_info by hash
          5361df2a2eb79e6a7e896ca10455af451a8cc5c78bc880245f228bd7242d8054.
  This is the COVERED order: it is spent by the filler repo's covered proof tx
  fe17fb88fe4282e133e980808b9e11fc92aa0f7fe1ee3f89f3ab7a77abe4d784 (which lists
  b6bcae...754cc#1 as an input with this exact datum hash). No output returns to
  the V3 address in the covered tx, so the coverage=Some datum survives only on the
  spent input -> captured here from the create tx.
  Sell 4.0 ADA -> buy 1000 FRENCHIE WIFF. coverage = Some(...) (Constr 0 / tag 121):
    beneficiary payment cred 63e326c9...df45ae (Constr 0), no stake part,
    a 100 field (coverage amount / min), and an all-zero seed-ref (index 0).
  min_partial_fill = 0.

Field breakdown (eyeballed from cbor2 decode)
---------------------------------------------
SwapDatum is a Constr-0 record. Two field orderings are seen depending on which
side is ADA:

  When ADA is the SELL side (b6bcae out0/1/2, live 18a01339):
    [ owner_address,
      sell_policy (empty = lovelace/ADA), sell_name (empty),
      sell_amount (int),
      buy_policy, buy_name, buy_amount (int),
      <Constr-1 flag>,
      seed_order_ref = Constr0(tx_hash bytes32, index int),
      min_partial_fill (int),
      coverage = Constr1 None | Constr0 Some(...) ]

  When a token is the SELL side (live ad182bcd, b6bcae out2):
    [ owner_address,
      buy_policy, buy_name, buy_amount (int),
      sell_policy (empty = ADA) ... ] etc. — i.e. the paid/received pair is
      ordered by which asset is ADA; confirm exact field semantics against the
      V3 on-chain SwapDatum definition when wiring the decoder.

  coverage sentinel:  Constr 1 (tag 122) = None ;  Constr 0 (tag 121) = Some.
  Only order_b6bcaeb6_out1_cov_some.hex has coverage = Some.

Provenance / how captured
-------------------------
  Live UTxOs:
    POST https://api.koios.rest/api/v1/address_utxos
      {"_addresses":["addr1z9sz8ava...szcetqsp0ume8"],"_extended":true}
    -> inline_datum.bytes on each UTxO.
  Create-tx datums (datum-hash outputs):
    POST https://api.koios.rest/api/v1/tx_info  {"_tx_hashes":["b6bcae...754cc"]}
      -> outputs at the V3 address carry datum_hash (not inline)
    POST https://api.koios.rest/api/v1/datum_info
      {"_datum_hashes":["630e47...","5361df...","7669735d..."]}  -> .bytes
  Covered-order confirmation:
    POST https://api.koios.rest/api/v1/tx_info
      {"_tx_hashes":["fe17fb...e4d784"],"_inputs":true}
      -> input b6bcae...754cc#1 with datum_hash 5361df... (the cov=Some order).

Proof txs (from the filler repo):
  create  b6bcaeb69401127ed650fea550c87464c7fed8aeef05f25950738db6ece754cc
  covered fe17fb88fe4282e133e980808b9e11fc92aa0f7fe1ee3f89f3ab7a77abe4d784
  partial ad182bcd7273ed7130ac22568ee9ddb0890f90db7040dd68e2bafa69342805b3

Do NOT commit these fixtures.
